[7] there was a little girl.

She was very small and very weak,
So weak that the doctor said,
"Little things are very hard,
For you to do."

So they took her outside,
To the fresh air and the bright sun,
And they put her on a bed,
Where she could get some rest.

When she was lying there,
She started to cry,
And tears fell from her eyes,
And they all fell on the ground.

But still they took her outside,
And gave her a chance,
To show her what she could do,
But she couldn't.

She didn't want to go,
And she didn't want to stay,
She just wanted to be home,
Where it's warm and cozy.

But they wouldn't let her,
No matter what she said,
They just kept saying,
"That's the way."

And she was very sad,
And she felt so blue,
Because no one would let her be,
Just the way it's always true.

