Once upon a time, in a tiny village, there lived a wise old man. He spent most of his days teaching his young friends the secrets of the universe.

One sunny afternoon, a curious little girl asked him, "What's the secret of the universe?"

The old man smiled and said, "Well, little one. The secret of the universe is that nothing happens. Always, everything is the same."

The little girl thought for a moment, then looked around at her friends. She saw that they were all thinking, "But what's that noise?!" or "I could do that!!" But no matter what they thought, they never actually did anything.

Finally, the little girl had an idea. "What if we all stop thinking about it for a minute?" she asked.

The old man thought for a moment. Then he nodded his head. "That's a good idea, little one."

And so they stopped thinking about what they thought,
