[4] I was at the zoo on a Saturday afternoon, and I had my daughter Emma here with me. She was bubbling over with excitement.

"I love zoos," she said.

I said, "I think zoos are pretty cool."

We walked up to the big elephant enclosure.

"Elephants really do love to eat," Emma said. They spend all day eating big big trunks full of yummy fruit.

We watched as they munched happily on some fruit. And they had lots of big soft beds where they could sleep.

After a while they got so sleepy they just rested in the big soft bed and slept all day.

