[6] I don't have a specific story to tell, but I was thinking of a time when I saw a woman who looked like she had just walked off a boat. She was wearing a yellow sundress and her hair was tied up in pigties. I couldn't tell if she was happy to see me or if she was just going about her day.

I walked up to her and said, "Well, hello there. You look just like the girl who used to live on this island." She said, "That's my home. I was born there."

I couldn't believe what I said. She told me that she had moved to the city when she was little. I asked her, "Did you ever play on that island?"

She said, "I loved to run around and jump in the waves. I was so happy to be able to do things like that."

I asked her, "Did you ever go back to the island?"

She said, "I couldn't.
[7] You could tell that this story was going to be good. It had all the makings of a classic: adventure, romance, and a happy ending.

