[10] There was once a little girl named Lily. She was very curious and loved to ask questions. One day she asked her mother, "What is the world like?"

Her mother replied, "You know how there's air around us?"

Lily thought for a moment and said, "And there's water?"

Her mother smiled and said, "You can go out into the backyard and see."

Lily ran outside and looked out at the sky. She saw that there were clouds floating above the trees. She asked her mother, "What are those?"

Her mother said, "They're just clouds."

Lily thought for a moment. She remembered what she had seen the day before. She asked her mother, "Do you think those clouds are going to rain?"

Her mother just laughed and said, "You think clouds are going to rain?"

Lily looked at the clouds and thought, "You say they're just clouds."

Just then, a loud clap of thunder boomed through the sky

